WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
Launch a probe straight up from a planet.

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:05.830
Ignore air resistance
and the planet's spin.

3
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.930
As it climbs, gravity pulls
it back, and it slows down.

4
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.610
Launch it gently and it
turns back and falls.

5
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.270
So how fast must a probe leave a
planet so that it never comes back?

6
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.100
Or does everything come back in the end?

7
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:25.200
In this mission, you'll track the probe's
energy as it climbs out of the planet's

8
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.280
gravity.

9
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.240
Then you'll test whether a heavier
probe needs a faster launch.

10
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:34.770
Your mission: find the launch speed
that means the probe never comes back.
